# NONE (no graphics, so SPOT never asks for a device) and OBS ALL / NEGATIVE / POSITIVE on the manual's
# Cassegrain (cmdref: Behavior Toggles).  Each OBS setting confirms itself; the spot's centroid is reported
# under each (the obscured rays are the 121 inside the secondary's shadow).
old $ROOT/docs/macos-manual/examples/Cassegrain.in
none
obs
all
spot 5
tout
obs
negative
spot 5
tout
obs
positive
spot 5
tout
# EXPECT: All rays plotted on spot diagrams[\s\S]*?Centroid of spot diagram[\s\S]*?Obscured rays only plotted on spot diagrams[\s\S]*?Centroid of spot diagram[\s\S]*?Unobscured rays only plotted on spot diagrams[\s\S]*?Centroid of spot diagram
# EXPECT: A total of\s+121 rays were lost\s+Obscured:\s+121
# EXPECT-NOT: Graphics device/type
# EXPECT-NOT: forrtl
